// Algorithm 1: RANSAC for plane fitting
Input: 3D points data;

For all $N_{rounds}$ DO
    Select three random points ($P_1, P_2, P_3$) from the input data;
    Fit a plane through the points;
    Set: $N_{inliers} = 0$;
    For all pints do
        If point distance to plane is within a threshold then ;
        Increment $N_{inliers}$;
        If $N_{inliers}$ is larger than the best plane then;
        Update plane estimation using all points;
        Update best plane;
    End

End

Output: Dominant plane;

// Algorithm 2: Region growing method for plane fitting
Input: 3D points data;

For all point DO

    S= two random neighbouring point $P_1, P_2$;

    Select nearest point $P_n$ within the certain distance;

    If the new added point $P_n$ does not change the plane estimation, then add this point $P_n$ into the selected date set S;

    If the size of S > certain threshold;

    The add plane estimate to set of planes;

End

Output: Set of planes;

